--- A. the setup: the band is 5 min, due_slack is 10 min
   band   | due_slack 
----------+-----------
 00:05:00 | 00:10:00

--- B. settle all twelve, then assert THE INVARIANT: next_poll_at > now() + due_slack, for every one
 settled | clear_of_slack | inside_slack_would_loop | every_gap_exceeds_slack | and_none_exceeds_slack_plus_band 
---------+----------------+-------------------------+-------------------------+----------------------------------
      12 |             12 |                       0 | t                       | t

--- C. and the behaviour that matters: primary_poll_due hands NONE of them back out
 due_right_after_settling 
--------------------------
                        0

--- D. axs_watch_next therefore hands out nothing either — this is the loop, closed
 handed_out 
------------
 []

--- E. the phase is still honoured: each next_poll_at is congruent to the event's own phase
 events | phase_aligned 
--------+---------------
     12 |            12

--- F. the gap never exceeds due_slack + one band, so freshness is not given away
 within_slack_plus_one_band 
----------------------------
 t

